[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Slip of the Tongue]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.50]Who made the only funny joke that evening and why? | 那天晚上唯一有趣的玩笑是谁开的？为什么？
[00:16.68]People will do anything to see a free show--even if it is a bad one. | 人们会想尽办法看一场免费演出——哪怕演得很糟糕。
[00:24.43]When the news got round that a comedy show would be presented | 当“P.&U.鸟食公司”将在我们当地电影院
[00:29.24]at our local cinema by the P. and U. Bird Seed Company, we all rushed to see it. | 演出一场喜剧的消息传开后，我们都赶紧跑去观看。
[00:37.11]We had to queue for hours to get in and there must have been several hundred people present just before the show began. | 我们不得不排了几个小时的队才进了场，开演前场内肯定有好几百人。
[00:47.17]Unfortunately, the show was one of the dullest we have ever seen. | 不幸的是，这次演出是我们看过的最乏味的演出之一。
[00:53.40]Those who failed to get in need not have felt disappointed, | 那些没能入场的人倒不必感到失望，
[00:59.06]as many of the artistes who should have appeared did not come. | 因为许多应该出场的演员都没有来。
[01:04.69]The only funny things we heard that evening came from the advertiser at the beginning of the programme. | 那天晚上我们听到的唯一有趣的事是节目开始时那位广告商的事。
[01:12.81]He was obviously very nervous and for some minutes stood awkwardly before the microphone. | 他显然非常紧张，在麦克风前局促不安地站了好几分钟。
[01:21.18]As soon as he opened his mouth, everyone burst out laughing. | 可他刚一开口说话，大家便哄堂大笑起来。
[01:27.76]We all know what the poor man should have said, | 我们都知道那个可怜的人本该说什么，
[01:31.48]but what he actually said was: 'This is the Poo and Ee Seed Bird Company. Good ladies, evening and gentlemen!' | 而他实际说的却是：“这是‘波一鸟食公司’。好女士们，晚上和先生们！”
